FILE _goals/convex-backend-runtime-2026-10-02/qa/task03c1/contracts.md:120
120: 
121: ## HTTP and private-fetch seams
122: 
123: Convex 1.46.0's `ConvexHttpClient.setAuth` accepts a static raw token and exposes
124: `clearAuth`. It has no automatic host getter callback. Use a dedicated HTTP client
125: and `credentials.withHttpAuth(client, operation, request?)` for each authenticated
126: invocation. The helper obtains the current token immediately before the operation,
127: calls `setAuth(token)` or `clearAuth()` for null, and invokes the operation once.
128: Concurrent operations using the same credential object/client are serialized across
129: auth attachment and operation completion. Use this helper for all authenticated calls
130: on that dedicated client; calls outside it or sharing the client among different
131: credential objects do not participate in its queue.
132: 
133: Getter rejection/invalid results cause zero HTTP authentication writes, operation
134: calls or wire requests. HTTP operation errors propagate unchanged. They do not
135: refresh and redispatch the operation, and they do not poison later explicit calls.
136: No silent retry is added for a mutation, paid request or external effect. An explicit
137: caller request can pass `{ forceRefreshToken: true }` without replaying another call.
138: 
139: `getAuthorizationHeaders(request?)` obtains a fresh current host token and returns
140: `{ Authorization: "Bearer <host JWT>" }`, or `{}` on null. These are auth headers for
141: one request; never merge a previous Authorization header back into a logout request.
142: Header creation performs no fetch, follows no redirect and returns no bytes. Task12
143: must bind actual private fetches to a trusted configured Convex origin/route, reject
144: untrusted asset URLs and redirects, and enforce independent storage authorization
145: and the 20,000,000-byte response cap. Never send this bearer credential to a remote
146: provider, raw storage bearer URL or user-supplied asset origin. Route validation and
147: private byte lifecycle are intentionally not inferred from a header helper.
148: 
149: ## Browser and downstream integration
150: 
151: The credential leaf module has only type imports from `convex/browser`. Its bundled
152: browser implementation has one source input, no Node/provider/backend modules and
153: no injected credentials. Its browser consumer compiles with `types: []` and only
154: ES2022/DOM libraries. The root package exports `HostCredentials`, `HostTokenFetcher`
155: and `HostTokenRequest`, plus `HostAuthFailure`/`HostAuthErrorHandler`. The retained
156: extracted-package runner now checks the new diagnostic declarations; the coordinator
157: must rebuild and execute it after this source freeze because shared build ownership
158: is serialized. Earlier package receipts cover the pre-review source snapshot only.
159: Task09 can reuse the live bound credential object for thin transports without
160: reintroducing model keys, token caches or a second client-owned agent loop.
161: 
162: Task03C2 must qualify actual signed host JWTs and identity changes against the
163: verified disposable service: reactive refresh/reconnect, cross-tenant subscription
164: denial, null/logout identity, forged/expired/missing issuer/audience/signature,
165: scoped tool execution and grant-revoked/deleted background outcomes. Task12/13 then
166: provide private byte/upload/storage-reference and authenticated callback negative
167: cases, trusted route binding and byte-cap outcomes. Mocked constructor tests, actual installed reactive manager/inert WebSocket tests
168: and HTTP-client requests with synthetic strings are transport plumbing evidence only.

